! ax5b_160_test2_ia.strap -- jb_ax5b "I-BOX 5", routine 1260
! ("----1260---CHECK MASK, INDICATOR, AND INTERRUPT.", banner PDF p.8),
! its TEST 2: "-TEST 2, CHK DATA IN IA." -- IBM's walk of a single
! one through the INTERRUPT ADDRESS register's bits 0-17.
!
!   PDF p.22     014556.00-014564.00  I6041: TEST 2's loop
!   PDF pp.22-23 014564.40-014617.00  I60B6: its error table, 18 entries
!                                     of three half-words each
!   PDF p.23     014617.40-014623.40  I6043: exit (B,SSW), continuity BIT3
!   PDF p.23     014624.00-014625.40  the clearing loop that falls into
!                                     TEST 3 (I6033, 014626.00, PDF p.24)
!   PDF p.114    024501.00-024546.00  the constant pool and BIT0-BIT20,
!                                     as decks/ax5b_bit_table.strap
!                                     transcribes them (verified there)
!
! No printed page numbers on these sheets: cited by PDF page and octal
! location.  Read from the page images at 150 dpi, and the code rows of
! pp.22-23 again at 400 dpi (every row agreed).  Checked row for row
! against the printed machine code by
! tests/verify_ax5b_160_test2_ia_listing.py (83 rows, 6 symbols).
!
! THE RULE.  Reference Manual printed p.48 (PDF p.51), "Interruption
! Address Register", read in the page image: "The interruption address
! register contains 18 bits and has address 2.0, which places it in the
! protected area of storage."  (The reference card's special-storage
! table agrees, word 2 bits 0-17: docs/microarchitecture_plan.md A.10,
! and STRAP's $IA in docs/c22_6531_appendix_a.md.)  The model holds it
! as interruptionAddress in bsv/StretchStorage.bsv, which keeps bits
! 0-17 of a store and drops 18-63 (see OBSERVATION below).
!
! ENTRY STATE.  IBM reaches I6041 by TEST 1C's "BD,$+.32" (014554.00),
! so TEST 2 runs with the interruption system DISABLED; the model resets
! disabled (StretchStorage.bsv's irqEn), so a run from END matches.
! "Protected area" is no obstacle disabled: printed p.31 (PDF p.35),
! "In the disabled mode, core storage protection as specified by the
! address boundary registers in conjunction with the boundary control
! bit does not take place" (as decks/sic_bd_protected_store.strap
! quotes it from the page image) -- and IBM's own test stores into word 2
! here, disabled, and expects the store to take.  So the model's
! unenforced protection of word 2 (its comment: "permanently protected
! on real HW; not enforced") is not exercised by this run: a store from
! the ENABLED state is not what TEST 2 tests.
!
! HOW TEST 2 WORKS.  X1 counts eighteen passes (LCI,$X1,18) and indexes
! the bit table: LV,$X3,BIT0($X1) loads BITk's value (bit k alone), SV
! stores it into IA's bits 0-24 and KV compares it back algebraically
! (Reference Manual printed p.24).  BXE is the pass path; a failure
! takes B,I60B6($X2), X2 stepping 1.32 words (three half-words) per
! pass, into the entry naming bit k.  CB+ advances X1 by a word to the
! next BITk.  Bits 18-24 are never written with a one: TEST 2 checks
! only that each of IA's eighteen bits holds a one by itself.
!
! The four rows after the continuity block (LCI/LVI/Z,0.0($X1)/CB+)
! zero words 0-15 and fall into TEST 3; they follow B,SSW, so the
! segment run never reaches them.  They are transcribed and verified.
!
! RESULT, 2026-11-19: the model PASSES IBM's checks (PC 1410 = SSW, SEN
! 0), run from END (I6041).  No disagreement with the listing.
! Final state, pinned in run_tests.sh: IA (word 2) = 0x400000000000, bit
! 17 alone (BIT17, the last pattern); X1 = 0x4800000000000, value 22.00
! (eighteen words: CB+ advanced it a word a pass), count 0; X2 =
! 0x6c00000000000, value 33.00 = 18 x 1.32; X3 = 0x400000000000, value
! 1.00 = BIT17's.  CYCLES 2057.  X values print the model's
! packIndexWord layout (value in bits 63-40); CYCLES is MODEL BEHAVIOUR.
!
! OBSERVATION, settled 2026-11-19: p.48 gives IA 18 bits, but the model
! kept all 64 bits of a store into word 2.  TEST 2 cannot see it (SV
! writes bits 0-24 and BIT0-BIT17 have nothing in 18-24).  The evidence
! is now decks/ia_width_18bit.strap, which stores ones into word 2 three
! ways and reads them back; with printed p.34's rule ("Those bit
! positions that are not so assigned are always zero") and p.35's "Bits
! 0-17 of location 2" the model now drops bits 18-63.  TEST 2's run is
! unchanged by the fix (same pins, same CYCLES).
!
! MODEL INJECTION, OBSERVED (a scratch copy of bsv/; the tracked bsv/
! never touched):
!   M1 IA bit 9 (BSV 54) dropped on a store: "interruptionAddress <= v &
!     ~(64'h1 << 54)" in StretchStorage.bsv's addrInterruptAddr arm ->
!     FAIL: PC 1416 (SERS), SEN 0x660c00000000000 (return 014603.00: the
!     SIC at 014602.00, "-IA DATA FAILURE, BIT 9.", p.23's first row),
!     IA 0, X1 0x2400000240000 (value 11.00 = nine words, count 9 left),
!     X2 0x3600000000000 (value 15.40 = 9 x 1.32), X3 0x40000000000000
!     (BIT9's value 400.00), CYCLES 1151.
!   CONTROL: the unmodified bsv/ in the same scratch copy: PASS, PC 1410,
!     SEN 0, IA/X1/X2/X3 as pinned, CYCLES 2057.  StretchStorage.bsv
!     restored from a saved copy; cmp IDENTICAL with the tracked file.
!
! SUBSTITUTIONS (not on these pages):
!   * SSIP's entry points at the addresses jb_ax4b PDF p.193's SYN table
!     prints, which these pages' own machine code repeats (SSW 1301.0,
!     SERS 1304.0, SEN 1310.0, SENO 1311.0): SSW a PASS halt, SERS a
!     FAIL halt, SEN/SENO data words SIC stores into, as in
!     decks/ax5b_160_test1ab_mask.strap.  TEST 2 is entered from TEST
!     1C's continuity block; it has no prologue of its own.
!   * IC260 (022737.00) is SYN'd at the address these pages' own machine
!     code prints for it ("LX,$X13,IC260" 22737.32 10).
!   * Notation only: "%" and the box glyph are "(" and ")"; the label
!     glyph the scan shows as "1" is the letter I.  p.23 prints the
!     clearing row as "Z,0.0.%$X1" (a period after 0.0); written
!     Z,0.0($X1), which assembles to the printed "0.22 01".

! ---- SSIP's entry points: SUBSTITUTES (not on these pages) -----------
        SLC, (8)1301.0
SSW     BEW, $                        ! SUBSTITUTE: PASS (the return to SSIP)
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $                        ! SUBSTITUTE: FAIL (SSIP's error report)
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0                ! SUBSTITUTE: SIC's error link word
SENO    DD(BU,64,8), 0                ! SUBSTITUTE: SIC's other link word
!
! ---- routine 1260's own label outside these pages, SYN'd at the
! address this listing prints for it (an input, not a witness) --------
IC260   SYN, (8)22737.0               ! -CONTINUITY REG 1260. (PDF p.83)
!
! ======================================================================
! PDF p.22, 014556.00-014601.40: TEST 2's loop and the first nine
! entries of its error table I60B6
! ======================================================================
        SLC, (8)14556.0
I6041   LVI, $X1, 0.0                 ! -TEST 2, CHK DATA IN IA.
        LCI, $X1, 18
        LVI, $X2, 0.0
I6041A  LV, $X3, BIT0($X1)
        SV, $X3, $IA
        NOP
        NOP
        KV, $X3, $IA
        BXE, $+1.0
        B, I60B6($X2)
I6042   V+I, $X2, 1.32
        CB+, $X1, I6041A
        BD, I6043
!
I60B6   SIC, SEN                      ! -IA DATA FAILURE, BIT 0.
        BD, SERS
        BD, I6042
!
        SIC, SEN                      ! -IA DATA FAILURE, BIT 1.
        BD, SERS
        BD, I6042
!
        SIC, SEN                      ! -IA DATA FAILURE, BIT 2.
        BD, SERS
        BD, I6042
!
        SIC, SEN                      ! -IA DATA FAILURE, BIT 3.
        BD, SERS
        BD, I6042
!
        SIC, SEN                      ! -IA DATA FAILURE, BIT 4.
        BD, SERS
        BD, I6042
!
        SIC, SEN                      ! -IA DATA FAILURE, BIT 5.
        BD, SERS
        BD, I6042
!
        SIC, SEN                      ! -IA DATA FAILURE, BIT 6.
        BD, SERS
        BD, I6042
!
        SIC, SEN                      ! -IA DATA FAILURE, BIT 7.
        BD, SERS
        BD, I6042
!
        SIC, SEN                      ! -IA DATA FAILURE, BIT 8.
        BD, SERS
        BD, I6042
!
! ======================================================================
! PDF p.23, 014602.00-014625.40: the last nine entries, the exit, and
! the clearing loop that falls into TEST 3 (I6033, 014626.00)
! ======================================================================
        SIC, SEN                      ! -IA DATA FAILURE, BIT 9.
        BD, SERS
        BD, I6042
!
        SIC, SEN                      ! -IA DATA FAILURE, BIT 10.
        BD, SERS
        BD, I6042
!
        SIC, SEN                      ! -IA DATA FAILURE, BIT 11.
        BD, SERS
        BD, I6042
!
        SIC, SEN                      ! -IA DATA FAILURE, BIT 12.
        BD, SERS
        BD, I6042
!
        SIC, SEN                      ! -IA DATA FAILURE, BIT 13.
        BD, SERS
        BD, I6042
!
        SIC, SEN                      ! -IA DATA FAILURE, BIT 14.
        BD, SERS
        BD, I6042
!
        SIC, SEN                      ! -IA DATA FAILURE, BIT 15.
        BD, SERS
        BD, I6042
!
        SIC, SEN                      ! -IA DATA FAILURE, BIT 16.
        BD, SERS
        BD, I6042
!
        SIC, SEN                      ! -IA DATA FAILURE, BIT 17.
        BD, SERS
        BD, I6042
!
I6043   B, $+1.0
        BD, I6041
        SIC, SENO+.32
        B, SSW                        ! -TO SSIP.
        BD, $+.32
!
        LX, $X13, IC260               ! -UPDATE CONTINUITY CHECK.
        V+, $X13, BIT3
        SX, $X13, IC260
        BD, $+.32
        LCI, $X1, 16.0
        LVI, $X1, 0.0
        Z, 0.0($X1)
        CB+, $X1, $-.32
!
! ======================================================================
! PDF p.114, 024501.00-024546.00: the common constants and BIT0-BIT20,
! as decks/ax5b_bit_table.strap transcribes them (verified there, row
! by row; SENO's SYN left out: SENO is substituted above).  BIT0-BIT17
! are the eighteen patterns TEST 2 writes into IA.
! ======================================================================
        SLC,(8)24501.0
I00LC   DD(BU,64,8),(8)0000011770025700000000
I00Z    XW,0,0,0,0
I00O    DD(BU,64,8),(8)1777777777777777777777
I00VO   XW,-(8)777777.77,0,0
I00CO   XW,0,(8)777777,0
        DD(BU,64,8),0,0,0
        DD(BU,64,8),0,0,0
        DD(BU,64,8),0,0,0
        DD(BU,64,8),0,0,0
BIT0    XW,(8)400000.00,0,0
BIT1    XW,(8)200000.00,0,0
BIT2    XW,(8)100000.00,0,0
BIT3    XW,(8)40000.00,0,0
BIT4    XW,(8)20000.00,0,0
BIT5    XW,(8)10000.00,0,0
BIT6    XW,(8)4000.00,0,0
BIT7    XW,(8)2000.00,0,0
BIT8    XW,(8)1000.00,0,0
BIT9    XW,(8)400.00,0,0
BIT10   XW,(8)200.00,0,0
BIT11   XW,(8)100.00,0,0
BIT12   XW,(8)40.00,0,0
BIT13   XW,(8)20.00,0,0
BIT14   XW,(8)10.00,0,0
BIT15   XW,(8)4.00,0,0
BIT16   XW,(8)2.00,0,0
BIT17   XW,(8)1.00,0,0
BIT18   XW,(8).40,0,0
BIT19   XW,(8).20,0,0
BIT20   XW,(8).10,0,0
        END, I6041
